(SECTION: QUANTITATIVE APTITUDE) Tj T*
(--------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(Q1. A and B can complete a piece of work in 12 days and 18 days respectively. They work together for 4 days, after which B is replaced by C. If the remaining work is completed by A and C in 4 days, in how many days can C alone complete the entire work?) Tj T*
(    A\) 36 days   B\) 48 days   C\) 24 days   D\) 30 days) Tj T*
(    Correct Answer: A) Tj T*
(    Explanation: Work = 36 units \(LCM of 12 and 18\). Efficiency of A = 3, B = 2. Together they do \(3+2\)*4 = 20 units in 4 days. Remaining work = 16 units. Completed by A and C in 4 days => A and C together do 4 units per day. Since A's efficiency is 3, C's efficiency = 4 - 3 = 1 unit/day. C alone can complete the work in 36/1 = 36 days.) Tj T*
T*
T*
(SECTION: GENERAL INTELLIGENCE & REASONING) Tj T*
(--------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(Q2. Select the set in which the numbers are related in the same way as are the numbers of the following sets: \(12, 18, 225\) and \(14, 16, 225\)) Tj T*
(    A\) \(11, 15, 169\)   B\) \(13, 17, 225\)   C\) \(15, 19, 289\)   D\) \(16, 22, 361\)) Tj T*
(    Correct Answer: C) Tj T*
(    Explanation: The pattern is: \(\(First number + Second number\) / 2\)² = Third number. \(\(12 + 18\) / 2\)² = 15² = 225. \(\(14 + 16\) / 2\)² = 15² = 225. For option C: \(\(15 + 19\) / 2\)² = 17² = 289.) Tj T*
T*
T*
(SECTION: ENGLISH COMPREHENSION) Tj T*
(--------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(Q3. Identify the option that rectifies the spelling error in the underlined word: The doctor advised him to maintain proper hfgene.) Tj T*
(    A\) hygeine   B\) hygiene   C\) higene   D\) hygiena) Tj T*
(    Correct Answer: B) Tj T*
(    Explanation: The correct spelling is 'hygiene'.) Tj T*
