(Q4. Under which Article of the Indian Constitution can a High Court issue writs for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights?) Tj T*
(    A\) Article 32   B\) Article 226   C\) Article 131   D\) Article 143) Tj T*
(    Correct Answer: B) Tj T*
(    Explanation: Article 226 empowers High Courts to issue writs, whereas Article 32 empowers the Supreme Court to do so.) Tj T*
T*
T*
(SECTION: QUANTITATIVE APTITUDE) Tj T*
(--------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(Q5. If x + 1/x = 4, then what is the value of xu + 1/xu?) Tj T*
(    A\) 724   B\) 728   C\) 736   D\) 740) Tj T*
(    Correct Answer: A) Tj T*
(    Explanation: x² + 1/x² = 4² - 2 = 14. x³ + 1/x³ = 4³ - 3\(4\) = 52. xu + 1/xu = \(x² + 1/x²\)\(x³ + 1/x³\) - \(x + 1/x\) = 14 * 52 - 4 = 728 - 4 = 724.) Tj T*
T*
T*
(SECTION: GENERAL AWARENESS) Tj T*
(--------------------------------------------------) Tj T*
(Q6. Who was the founder of the Sunga Dynasty, which succeeded the Maurya Dynasty?) Tj T*
(    A\) Pushyamitra Sunga   B\) Agnimitra Sunga   C\) Vasumitra Sunga   D\) Devabhuti) Tj T*
(    Correct Answer: A) Tj T*
(    Explanation: Pushyamitra Sunga founded the Sunga Dynasty in 185 BC after assassinating Brihadratha, the last Mauryan ruler.) Tj T*
